WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.880
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today, I’m&nbsp;
going to explain a science fiction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.680
action film called “The Discovery.” 
Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
 
&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.880
At the beginning of the movie, we see&nbsp;
professor Thomas Harbor being interviewed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.560
He has recently proven the existence of life after&nbsp;
death. The interviewer claims that his discovery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.840
was dangerous, because ever since his work was&nbsp;
published, the suicide rate has been skyrocketing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.480
He dismisses the claim by saying that such a&nbsp;
crucial truth about human life had to be brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.000
to people, regardless the consequences. Thomas&nbsp;
has been able to capture brain wavelengths on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.440
subatomic level leaving a person’s body when they&nbsp;
die. This explains that a person’s consciousness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.160
goes somewhere when they die. But the interviewer&nbsp;
insists that since they do not know where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.760
consciousness goes, they cannot tell for sure if&nbsp;
the afterlife exists. Thomas tackles the claim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.560
saying that when a train leaves the station, we&nbsp;
know it is going somewhere. She then brings up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:03.600
that many celebrities, athletes, and hundreds of&nbsp;
civilians have ended their lives because of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.880
professor and asks him if he feels responsible&nbsp;
for their deaths. Thomas simply answers that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.720
doesn’t. Just then, one of the camera crew stands&nbsp;
before Thomas and thanks him for a “fresh start”.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:20.240
He shoots himself dead right after. In a similar&nbsp;
fashion, people have been committing mass suicide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.920
to restart a new life in the afterlife. 
It is now the second anniversary of the discovery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.880
Thomas’s son, Will Harbor is traveling on&nbsp;
a ferry, listening to a TV program talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.480
about his father’s discovery. As it turns out,&nbsp;
the suicide rate has not decreased ever since.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.760
Will turns the TV off, making it clear that he is&nbsp;
not proud of his father’s work. A girl from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:48.000
other seat startles him. They are the only ones on&nbsp;
the ferry. She introduces herself as Isla and Will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.200
comments that her face looks very familiar. The&nbsp;
two chitchat for a while. The conversation turns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.080
to them talking about the discovery. Isla is a&nbsp;
supporter of it, but Will exclaims that he doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:03.120
believe in it. Isla claims that the discovery gives&nbsp;
people a way to get relief from the sufferings of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:09.200
life, but Will stays adamant about his view. After&nbsp;
they get off the ferry, Isla hitchhikes in a car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.040
leaving Will at the harbor. His brother Toby comes&nbsp;
to pick him up. The two drive to a huge mansion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.760
bought by their father. Thomas has built his new&nbsp;
station in the mansion, and has employed people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:26.400
who survived attempted suicides. Will is confused&nbsp;
to see labs and machinery inside the house. Thomas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.760
has been conducting some kind of experiment. 
Will meets his father and bluntly asks him to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.200
all this. He wants Thomas to tell the media that&nbsp;
his discovery was false and stop the chain of mass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.480
suicides. Thomas laughs at his idea and claims&nbsp;
that his discovery was a hundred percent true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.840
and he won’t lie to anyone. As it turns out,&nbsp;
Will was the inspiration for the discovery.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.160
When Will was young he had an accident and&nbsp;
died for a minute. When he was resuscitated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:57.600
he had told his parents that he saw flashes and a&nbsp;
little boy in front of him. This provided Thomas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:02.320
with the idea that life after death might&nbsp;
exist. Hence, Will blames himself for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.840
deaths and wants his father to stop. After the&nbsp;
conversation, Will goes outside to cool his mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:13.520
but just then, he sees Isla on the beach nearby.&nbsp;
She seems to be packing her bags with weights.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:18.880
Isla wears the heavy bag and goes into the sea.&nbsp;
Will realizes she is about to commit suicide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:24.160
and runs to save her. He goes into the water&nbsp;
and manages to save her, but Isla is furious.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.600
He takes her to the mansion and asks Toby to take&nbsp;
her in, since they help people who are suicidal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.400
Toby agrees but she will have to go through&nbsp;
the questionnaire first. Isla is surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.120
to discover Thomas is Will’s father.
Thomas then conducts an interview with Isla,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:44.000
asking her questions about her life. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
Will goes around the house and sees that it has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.120
been fully converted into an establishment&nbsp;
with canteens and rooms for every patient.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:53.600
At night, everyone gathers in a room while&nbsp;
Thomas presents something to them. He brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:58.400
out a man with a device attached to his head&nbsp;
and claims that he has figured out a way to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:04.000
the afterlife. Till now, the world only knew that&nbsp;
our brain waves leave for somewhere after we die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.040
but now he has figured out a way to see where&nbsp;
the brain wavelengths go. Will and the others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.840
are shocked. Thomas explains that with the device,&nbsp;
they can see a video recording of the afterlife.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:19.520
Later, everyone is at Thomas’s office. He wants&nbsp;
to be the first one to be experimented upon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:24.400
but he has to be dead for that. Hence, they&nbsp;
decide to perform it on an already dead person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.600
which they have to steal from the morgue. On their&nbsp;
way there, Toby reveals to Isla that their mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:35.200
committed suicide and Will blames his father for&nbsp;
it. At the morgue, Toby distracts the keeper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:39.360
letting Will and Isla to successfully steal&nbsp;
a corpse of a man named Philips.
 
&nbsp;

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.480
That night, Will and Isla sleep on a bunk bed&nbsp;
together. Will tells her that his mother killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:48.400
herself on the day of his parents’ wedding&nbsp;
anniversary. His father was never attentive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:53.360
and she was left hopeless when Thomas didn’t come&nbsp;
out of his office on their anniversary. Will had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:58.640
found her dead body in the bathtub the following&nbsp;
morning. The two talk for a while and sleep, while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:04.240
holding hands. The next day, everyone is ready to&nbsp;
perform the experiment. They attach the corpse’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.280
head to the device and hit a button. While Thomas&nbsp;
waits for something to show on the monitor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:15.040
nothing happens. They do it repeatedly, but to&nbsp;
no avail. A disappointed Thomas leaves the room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:20.640
and everyone else follows. However, when Will is&nbsp;
alone inside, the monitor starts working and shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:25.840
a clip of Philips meeting a woman at a hospital.&nbsp;
Will quickly turns it off before Thomas comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:31.600
in again. They have to let Philips’s body go for&nbsp;
cremation and Thomas asks Toby for a new corpse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.560
Will and Isla take the corpse back to the&nbsp;
morgue and leave it on the ground outside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.680
All of a sudden, Isla kisses Will, the two are&nbsp;
awkward later and do not talk on the ride home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:46.960
Will cannot get the thought of the video out of&nbsp;
his head. He has downloaded it to his laptop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:50.960
After some research on the internet,&nbsp;
he finds the hospital in the video. 
&nbsp;

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.720
Will dives to the hospital and walks&nbsp;
through the passage Philips had walked.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:00.000
However, he reaches a dead end that was not in&nbsp;
the video. A janitor informs him that there used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.040
to be a passage before the hospital was renovated&nbsp;
a decade ago. Will realizes that the video could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.360
not have been from the future, he predicts&nbsp;
it to be Philips’s memories displaying on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.400
the monitor. His father had made a memory device&nbsp;
rather than something that shows the afterlife.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:15.200
Later, everyone gathers at the mansion for a&nbsp;
session, when Thomas calls a patient named Lacey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:20.160
to the stage. Lacy has been speaking against&nbsp;
the discovery and Thomas’s new invention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:25.360
claiming that it will cause more mass suicides.&nbsp;
Thomas confronts her in front of everyone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:29.120
As it turns out, he had found Lacy&nbsp;
in the woods ready to kill herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:34.080
and had saved her. In the end, he asks her&nbsp;
to pack her bag and leave the establishment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.960
Will is furious at Thomas for embarrassing&nbsp;
Lacey, but Thomas dismisses the matter. 
&nbsp;

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:44.560
Later, Will shows Isla Philps’s video. The two go&nbsp;
to the same hospital to investigate Philips's case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:49.840
together. They find Philips’s father’s file with&nbsp;
his address on it. They believe that in the video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:54.880
Philips was visiting his father on his deathbed&nbsp;
and the woman he met was probably a relative. 
&nbsp;

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:59.280
Later that night, Will has a chat with Toby who&nbsp;
tells him that Thomas has been working on this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.080
machine for their mother. Thomas is guilt-ridden&nbsp;
because of his wife’s death and wants to know she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:09.440
went to a better place. The following day, Will&nbsp;
and Isla go to the beach, where Isla tells him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:14.160
that her five-year-old son had died by drowning&nbsp;
in a beach because she fell asleep. That was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:19.280
the reason she wanted to die before Will saved&nbsp;
her. The two then go to Philips’s house and meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:23.760
his sister who happens to be the woman from the&nbsp;
video. She informs them that Philips never came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.720
to meet her father at the hospital. None of his&nbsp;
family likes him, as he had been awful to them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:33.280
Will has noticed a tattoo of a lighthouse on&nbsp;
Philips’s arm in the video but the woman tells him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:38.960
that he had a wave tattoo instead. Will realizes&nbsp;
the video is not Philips’s memory but rather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:43.440
his afterlife. Philips has gone back&nbsp;
in time to correct his mistakes in life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:48.080
after his death. As it turns out, in the&nbsp;
afterlife, people relive an alternate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:52.080
version of their life and get a second&nbsp;
chance to make different choices. 
&nbsp;

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:57.120
Will and Isla are surprised by the discovery. They&nbsp;
are in their room when suddenly, Toby barges in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:01.760
and calls them to see Thomas. Thomas has attached&nbsp;
himself to the device to try to figure out the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:07.600
machine. He has suffocated himself and is on the&nbsp;
verge of death. The monitor starts working again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:12.560
This time, it shows Thomas on the night of his&nbsp;
wife’s death. It was their anniversary. He had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:16.800
not come out of his office that day, but in the&nbsp;
video, he tells his wife that work can wait and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.760
has dinner with her. He had been given a&nbsp;
chance to correct his mistake, and he did.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:26.000
Right after watching the video, they unplug&nbsp;
the machine and bring Thomas back to life by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.600
electrocuting him with a defibrillator. Thomas is&nbsp;
shocked and delighted to see his device work. 
&nbsp;

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:36.560
It turns out that when a person dies, he goes back&nbsp;
to a time in his life that he regrets the most,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:39.360
and gets a second chance to&nbsp;
make different choices. 
&nbsp;

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:43.760
He gathers everyone in the house in the front&nbsp;
yard and is about to tell them about the invention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:48.160
when suddenly, a gunshot is heard. Lacey,&nbsp;
who has been kicked out of the mansion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:53.040
has shot Isla. She claims that she didn’t kill&nbsp;
her, just gave her a new beginning before being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:58.080
taken away by Toby. Isla falls to the ground and&nbsp;
tells Will that she doesn’t want to die anymore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.360
Will is devastated when she takes&nbsp;
her last breath in his arms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:06.480
Sometime later, we see Toby and Thomas talk&nbsp;
about Isla’s family for a police report.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.400
Thomas decides to destroy the machine after&nbsp;
seeing the impact it has on people.
&nbsp;

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.280
But when Thomas tries going inside his lab, he&nbsp;
discovers that it is locked from the inside.
&nbsp;

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:20.000
Will locks himself, and attaches himself&nbsp;
to the device. He suffocates himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.920
and when he is on the verge of death, Will&nbsp;
finds himself in a memory of himself back on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:29.440
the ferry. Will meets Isla again and asks her what&nbsp;
is going on. Isla reveals that this is a memory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:34.960
because Will is connected to the machine and is&nbsp;
not yet dead. Isla here is his own subconscious. 
&nbsp;

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:40.000
In the memory, Isla reveals that he has been&nbsp;
living this part in loops in multiple lives.The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:45.520
two first met on the same ferry many lives ago. 
But in that scenario, Will didn’t see Isla trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:50.080
to commit suicide, and couldn’t save her. When&nbsp;
he read about her death the following day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:54.560
he was filled with guilt because he knows he&nbsp;
could’ve done something on the ferry. He went on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:59.680
living his life but the guilt always remained with&nbsp;
him. Eventually, when he died, he was brought back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:04.640
to the ferry where he met Isla again, because&nbsp;
he regretted this moment the most in his life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:10.000
However, Will couldn’t save her even then. 
In the similar way, Will has been stuck in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:15.280
loop and lived his life hundreds of times trying&nbsp;
to save Isla. But he'd never been successful until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:20.960
his most recent life. Will has met her numerous times,&nbsp;
so a part of his consciousness remembers her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:24.080
That is why Isla looked familiar&nbsp;
to him when they first met.
&nbsp;

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:28.400
Isla tells him that since he has been able to&nbsp;
stop Isla from committing suicide in this life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:33.120
he has made peace with his consciousness and&nbsp;
has no regrets now. Also because of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:38.400
he would now end up somewhere else in his next&nbsp;
life, and not on the ferry. Will promises that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:43.680
in his next life, he will remember Isla. 
Just then, he begins to hear the voices of Thomas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:49.120
and Toby. They are trying to jump-start his heart,&nbsp;
but their attempt is unsuccessful and Will dies. 
&nbsp;

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:54.560
After he dies, his afterlife takes him back to&nbsp;
a beach. Will sees a little boy is alone playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:59.520
in the water. He takes him out, making sure the&nbsp;
kid doesn’t drown. Just then, Isla comes running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:05.040
to them, and we see that the kid is Isla’s son.&nbsp;
Will now has been sent to save him. Isla thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:09.760
him and walks away with her son. Neither of them&nbsp;
recognize the other. As Will walks away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:14.800
he turns around with a confused look on his face,&nbsp;
suggesting that he is starting to remember Isla. 
&nbsp;

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:18.560
The movie ends, but we can imagine&nbsp;
that Will perhaps asks Isla out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:23.600
coffee or something afterwards. 
